                                    <h1>Insurance Software Development: India &amp; UAE Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>Insurance is quietly one of the largest digital transformation categories — legacy carriers running 20-year-old PAS systems, insurtech disruptors building fully digital, and regulated markets demanding both compliance and customer experience. Here is what modern insurance software looks like across the stack.</p>
                                    <h2>The Insurance Software Stack</h2>
                                    <ol><li><strong>Quote engine</strong> — real-time rate calculation across products.</li><li><strong>Policy administration system (PAS)</strong> — issue, renew, endorse, cancel.</li><li><strong>Agent / broker portal</strong> — quote, bind, commission tracking.</li><li><strong>Customer portal / app</strong> — view policies, file claims, pay premiums.</li><li><strong>Claims management</strong> — FNOL, adjuster workflow, settlement.</li><li><strong>Fraud detection</strong> — pattern recognition, anomaly detection.</li><li><strong>Underwriting workbench</strong> — data-driven risk assessment.</li><li><strong>Regulatory reporting</strong> — IRDAI / CBUAE / FCA / NAIC filings.</li></ol>
                                    <h2>Build vs Buy</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Enterprise PAS:</strong> Guidewire, Duck Creek, Majesco. Deep, expensive, long implementations. $2M-50M.<br><strong>Mid-market:</strong> Insurity, EIS, InsureCert, PolicyCore.<br><strong>India-first:</strong> RIA, InsureMO, BASYS. ₹2-40 Cr.<br><strong>Custom:</strong> Right for insurtech disruptors, specialty lines, or unique models. ₹1.5-10 Cr build.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost + Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>MVP customer-facing app (16-24 weeks):</strong> ₹40-90 lakh / $48K-108K.<br><strong>Full digital insurance platform (24-48 weeks):</strong> ₹2-6 Cr / $240K-720K.<br><strong>Enterprise PAS replacement (36-72 weeks):</strong> ₹5-25 Cr / $600K-3M.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Regulation</h2>
                                    <p><strong>India:</strong> IRDAI regulations, PoSP (Point of Sale Person) framework, Bima Sugam upcoming.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> Central Bank UAE (recently absorbed Insurance Authority), ADGM / DIFC regulations for offshore insurers.<br><strong>USA:</strong> State-by-state (all 50). NAIC standards. Highly fragmented.<br><strong>UK:</strong> FCA + PRA regulations, Consumer Duty rules, ICOBS handbook.<br><strong>Saudi Arabia:</strong> SAMA regulation, growing InsurTech sandbox.</p>
                                    <h2>AI in Insurance</h2>
                                    <p>Underwriting risk scoring, claims fraud detection, damage assessment from photos (computer vision), chatbot-based FNOL, and automated document processing (medical records, police reports, invoices). Well-scoped AI in insurance delivers 30-60% claims processing cost reduction + 15-40% loss ratio improvement on high-fraud lines.</p>

